# 4. TEXT

_publ_section_synopsis
;\
In three
5-acetyl-11-ethyl-6,11-dihydro-5<i>H</i>-dibenzo[<i>b</i>,<i>e</i>]azepine-6-\
carboxylic acids, which differ only in the presence of zero, one or two
methyl substituents in one of the aryl rings, the hydrogen-bonded
supramolecular aggregation is respectively, two-, one- and three-dimensional.
;

_publ_section_keywords
;
crystal structure, dibenzo[<i>b</i>,<i>e</i>]azepine-6-carboxylic acid,
hydrogen bonding, hydrogen-bonded supramolecular aggregation
;

